---
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site'
import { uiClasses } from '../config/ui'
---
<section class="mt-20 w-full max-w-screen-lg border-t border-orange-950/10 pt-10 sm:mt-28 sm:pt-12" aria-labelledby="product-overview-title">
  <h2 id="product-overview-title" class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Built for your terminal workflow.</h2>
  <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-600">vibe hud keeps local AI coding sessions in a native Mac notch HUD. It brings together session status, conversation history, tool requests, and replies so you can follow several tasks while your terminal stays in the background.</p>
  <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-6 border-y border-orange-950/10 py-6 text-sm sm:grid-cols-3">
    <div><dt class="font-semibold text-stone-800">Requirements</dt><dd class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-stone-600">macOS {siteConfig.minimumMacOS} or later and a supported coding agent.</dd></div>
    <div><dt class="font-semibold text-stone-800">Your setup</dt><dd class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-stone-600">Terminal.app, iTerm2, Ghostty, and tmux workflows. Available actions depend on your agent and terminal.</dd></div>
    <div><dt class="font-semibold text-stone-800">Purchase</dt><dd class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-stone-600">{siteConfig.priceLabel} as a one-time purchase. <a class={uiClasses.contactLink} href="/pricing/">Pricing details</a></dd></div>
  </dl>
  <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-x-7 gap-y-4 text-sm">
    <a class={uiClasses.contactLink} href="/docs/">Set up vibe hud</a>
    <a class={uiClasses.contactLink} href="/docs/claude-code/">Use with Claude Code</a>
    <a class={uiClasses.contactLink} href="/docs/codex/">Use with Codex</a>
    <a class={uiClasses.contactLink} href="/docs/compatibility/">Check compatibility</a>
  </div>
</section>
